    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers, and cascaded that new identity through every value derived from it.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** (the code generator):\n- Rewrote `generateCustomerCode` to return `<REGION>-<HASH8>`.\n- `deriveRegion(owner)` \u2014 region code derived from the postcode (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), falling back to the fixed city table, else `UNKNOWN`.\n- `hash8(owner)` \u2014 first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n- Removed the now-unused `prefix3` helper and the old sequence-counting logic.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** (the derived read-only fields):\n- `formatMembershipNumber` and `formatCheckDigit` already read straight off `customerCode`, so they now automatically build on the region-and-hash identity (I only updated the membership-number javadoc example, e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`).\n- `formatLocality` now derives the locality from the customer code's `REGION` segment (the part before the first `-`), so locality \"moves to\" the new identity rather than re-deriving independently. Removed the mapper's obsolete `CITY_REGION`/`REGION_POSTCODES` tables.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the create audit record (`auditLogger.info(\"owner created: ... customerCode={} ...\")`) reads `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now logs the new identity with no change needed (verified in the run: `AUDIT - owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...`).\n\nThe `PostcodeValidator` keeps its own independent region tables (used only for input validation of the postcode-vs-city rule), so I left it untouched.\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
