    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe refactor is structurally clean and idiomatic:\n\n- **Region-derivation logic lives in the right unit now.** `CITY_REGION`/`REGION_POSTCODES` and the postcode-then-city fallback moved out of `OwnerMapper` (a MapStruct read-model mapper) into `ClinicServiceImpl`, which is the component that actually *builds* the identity in `generateCustomerCode`. Deriving the region where the customer code is minted is the natural home.\n\n- **Duplication was eliminated, not relocated.** The old code had the region tables in the mapper; the new `formatLocality` no longer re-derives region from postcode/city at all \u2014 it parses the region segment back out of the already-computed `customerCode`. So the region rules exist in exactly one place (`deriveRegion`), and locality is guaranteed to agree with the identity by construction. That's a better factoring than before.\n\n- **Helpers are cohesive and appropriately scoped.** `deriveRegion(Owner)` and `hash8(Owner)` are private static helpers sitting alongside `generateCustomerCode`, each doing one thing. `generateCustomerCode` reads as a clean two-part composition. This doesn't turn `ClinicServiceImpl` into a catch-all \u2014 it's the same identity-generation responsibility the class already owned, just re-expressed.\n\n- **Membership number and downstream values follow automatically** because they were already built from `customerCode`; only the doc example needed updating, which it was.\n\nMinor, non-blocking observation (not requesting changes): the two `static final` maps are inserted mid-class rather than grouped with the other class fields at the top \u2014 some maintainers prefer constants hoisted \u2014 but keeping them adjacent to their sole consumer (`deriveRegion`) is a defensible locality-of-behavior choice and reads fine.",
